Brigand wrote:
> Any advice?? Or does luck need to be with me as well as skill?

There are very few situations that are COMPLETELY unpreventable. A long 
string of bad luck should be about the only thing that does you in and 
the better you get, the longer the string will have to be before it 
kills you. Every time you die think HARD about what could have saved you 
and why it didn't.

Almost all deaths to monsters can be avoided with the E-word, a wand of 
digging, and other common equipment. Don't kill monsters when you can 
avoid them. When you go down a level, it's prudent to engrave on the 
upstairs before anything else, then just wait several turns to see if 
any dangers approach.

Equipment is a priority. Don't do anything you can't handle until you've 
got some decent equipment. Dipping for Excalibur, for example, can be 
dangerous, so be prepared for ANY of the consequences. Pet-test all the 
armor you find and try it on; you have pretty good odds of finding a +3 
in there.

Until you can handle all traps, step on as few squares as possible, 
especially in the mines. When you can, tread where a pet or monster has 
already been.

